      "claim": "The Married Women's Property Act was passed in 1870.",
      "answer": "1870",
      "quote": "The Married Women 's Property Act 1870 provided that wages and property which a wife earned through her own work or inherited would be regarded as her separate property and by the Married Women 's Property Act 1882 , this principle was extended to all property , regardless of its source or the time of its acquisition .",
